# VFBCAI Cursor context (synced 2026-08-10)

## Priority
- GOAL1 first: CHECK / VERIFY / REGISTER / expert request / CRM / admin / mypage / notifications stability.
- No large new features (payments, OCR, Digital Vault, business member) before GOAL1 ships.

## Immutable principles
- Engine: CHECK → VERIFY → REGISTER → PROTECT (do not rename/reorder).
- No prices on customer UI.
- Customer-facing expert label: "VFBCAI 전문가팀" only (no real names / external org names).
- Prefer full-file replacements when Ace requests file delivery; one feature at a time; confirm before coding.

## Anonymous /ai channel structure (2026-08-10)
Three independent layers — do NOT make chat a teaser that forces clicking articles:
1. **Chat (`/ai`)**: Self-contained answer (full doc list + process + legal basis via `legalRagBasis.ts`). Article link is optional "더 자세히 보기", not required.
2. **Articles (`/answers/*`)**: SEO/AEO landing; not a mandatory hop from chat.
3. **Funnel (`/check/*`, etc.)**: Story + conversion; personalized diagnosis.

## Legal content policy
- Expert pre-review only for paid expert/agency cases — NOT for anonymous chat, diagnoses, `/answers/*`, SNS.
- Never invent articles/facts. Grade A/B/C from legal-rag (`answer_policy`) is the source for citations.
- `legalRagBasis.ts` (5s timeout) applies to TRC and all anonymous CHECK/VERIFY/REGISTER chat paths.
- External sources: whitelist only, must be fetched (not name-only), include fixed expert-consult disclaimer when used.

## PR #12 branch notes
- Branch: `cursor/anonymous-ai-fast-guide-cbde`
- Do not deploy `/answers/*` static pages without Ace confirming expert review (4-1); can feature-flag if needed.
- Intent routing: one canonical article per intent (not per question URL).

